# component: textarea
# decisions: API-26, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-3, FOC-5, FOC-6, FOC-8, FOC-14, API-40
# hunks:
#   FOC-1, FOC-3, FOC-6, FOC-8: `outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-3
#     focus-visible:ring-ring/50` becomes `outline-hidden` plus `focus:border-ring/70` — the
#     text-entry border tint on `:focus`, and no glow.
#   FOC-5: the invalid tint becomes `not-focus:aria-invalid:border-destructive` (and its dark
#     counterpart), so focus outranks it; the `aria-invalid` halo rings go with the rest.
#   API-26: the `<textarea>` renders through Base UI `Field.Control` (`render={<textarea />}`),
#     so inside a `Field` it takes the label, the rendered description and error ids, and
#     `aria-invalid` from the Field, like Base UI's own Input; outside a `Field` nothing is wired
#     (it still carries a generated `id`, exactly as Base UI's Input does).
#     `Field.Control` is hook-backed, so the file gains `"use client"` (API-16's lowest leaf).
#   FOC-14 (supersedes the FOC-3 border tint and FOC-5 above): no `focus:` border tint and no `not-
#     focus:` guard on the invalid border — the border never changes on focus (base.css's background
#     tint is the cue), and the invalid border holds in every state.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
#   FOC-14 text-entry exception (MK 2026-09-27; supersedes the FOC-14 note above for text
#     entry): text entry takes NO fill — base.css excludes text inputs and textarea from the
#     tint — and shows focus as a subtle darker border that eases in: `focus:not-aria-invalid:border-ring/50`,
#     with `transition-[color,background-color,border-color] duration-150 ease-out`. The
#     `not-…invalid` guard keeps an invalid field's destructive border in every state.
#   API-40 (MK blanket approval 27-10-2026 (D19), Regent product-cohesion UXT-23): the classes move
#     into `textareaVariants` (cva) with `variant` (`default` = upstream's bordered field, `ghost` =
#     borderless, transparent, one row, no resize) and `size` (`default` = upstream's type size, `lg`
#     = heading size), reflected as `data-variant`/`data-size`; `submitOnEnter` makes Enter submit
#     the form (Shift+Enter and IME composition untouched — `isComposing` or `keyCode` 229, the
#     composition-ending Enter); a ghost textarea grows with its text by
#     a measured height where the browser lacks `field-sizing: content`.
